# ---- 7 API/UI
add("<h2 class='pb'>7. API, UI and deployment</h2><p>Backend: FastAPI (<code>api/main.py</code>) with <code>GET /health</code>, <code>GET /trips</code>, <code>POST /predict</code>. The prediction path (<code>Predictor.predict</code>) reads only .track/.nodes/.arcs; the reference .route is read only by the server-side <code>evaluate()</code>, and only metrics and the predicted route are returned to the UI. UI: single-page Leaflet app (<code>ui/index.html</code>) listing the trips from the API. Run instructions: README.md.</p>" + img("ui_screenshot.png") + "<p>Screenshot of the working UI (student-test trip, API on localhost).</p>" + img("api_log_screenshot.png", "85%") + "<p>Captured API server log showing the requests and results (real <code>uvicorn</code> output from <code>results/api.log</code>). </p><h3>7.1 Two-laptop test</h3><p>Laptop 1 (Mac) ran the FastAPI server on the evaluator trips (<code>EVAL_DIR=.../evaluator_test uvicorn api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000</code>). Laptop 2 (Windows) ran the UI (<code>python -m http.server 8080</code> in <code>ui/</code>) with the API URL pointing to laptop 1 over the local network. Below: the Mac terminal receiving the request from the Windows laptop (client address 10.8.120.179) and the Windows browser showing the returned route and metrics for evaluator trip 00000023.</p>" + img("twolaptop_api_terminal_mac.png") + "<p>Laptop 1 terminal: <code>POST /predict trip_id=00000023</code> followed by the result line and <code>200 OK</code>.</p>" + img("twolaptop_ui_windows.png", "85%") + "<p>Laptop 2 UI: predicted route (red) over GPS (blue), with classifier and classifier+HMM metrics.</p>")
add("<h2>8. Limitations and integrity statement</h2><ul><li>Labels come from our alignment of fixes to the reference route; reference routes are not independently verified (trips 33 and 54 clearly disagree with GPS).</li><li>Student-test has only 10 trips; differences below about one percentage point are not reliable.</li><li>Evaluator data was not available during development and was never used for features, models, hyperparameters or thresholds. Predictions are computed from raw GPS and network files only; nothing is hard-coded.</li></ul></body></html>")
